flowchart TD
  classDef works fill:#1d2029,stroke:#555b68,color:#eceef1;
  classDef friction fill:#262a34,stroke:#eceef1,stroke-width:2px,color:#eceef1;
  classDef broken fill:#1d2029,stroke:#d77757,stroke-width:2px,color:#d77757;
  classDef byhand fill:#1d2029,stroke:#eceef1,stroke-width:1px,stroke-dasharray:4 3,color:#eceef1;
  S1["1. The releases page offers the zip of each<br/>version and its .sha256; the README says it<br/>runs on a Mac with Apple silicon (M1 or later)<br/>on macOS 14 or later.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S2["2. In Terminal, shasum -a 256 -c checks the zip<br/>and prints OK; unzip and move tokenpanda.app to<br/>Applications.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S3["3. With Homebrew instead: brew install --cask<br/>tokenpandadev/tap/tokenpanda, with no trust<br/>step; the cask declares Apple silicon only, so<br/>an Intel Mac is refused, and the caveats say<br/>Open Anyway and explain the zap.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S4["4. Double click in Applications: macOS refuses the<br/>ad hoc build, 'Apple could not verify<br/>tokenpanda is free of malware'.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S5["5. System Settings, Privacy and Security, scroll<br/>to the bottom, Open Anyway.<br/><i>by hand</i>"]:::byhand
  S6["6. The warning comes back once; Open Anyway starts<br/>the app.<br/><i>by hand</i>"]:::byhand
  S7["7. No notification prompt at launch: the app asks<br/>when the first nudge is due, or when Nudge or<br/>Reopen sessions is ticked.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S8["8. The menu bar shows the panda alone at half<br/>strength: no figures yet. No window, no Dock<br/>icon.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S9["9. If the icon is not on screen five seconds after<br/>the first launch, one window: 'tokenpanda is<br/>running'. From macOS 26 the icon 'may be<br/>switched off in System Settings, Menu Bar,<br/>hidden behind the notch when the menu bar is<br/>full, or kept out of view by an app that hides<br/>menu bar icons, such as Bartender or Ice', with<br/>'Open Menu Bar Settings' and 'OK'; before macOS<br/>26 the menu bar is 'most likely' full, quitting<br/>another menu bar app makes room, and a menu bar<br/>manager can also keep the icon out of view,<br/>with 'OK' only. The notch is named only on a<br/>Mac with one: with no notch the text says 'left<br/>out when the menu bar is full', and when it is<br/>not known (a connected screen has a notch, the<br/>item's screen is not known) both causes are<br/>named. While the screen is locked, the session<br/>is switched away or the display sleeps, it<br/>waits and asks again. It shows once.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S10["10. Switching the item on in System Settings, Menu<br/>Bar, is the user's click.<br/><i>by hand</i>"]:::byhand
  S1 --> S2
  S2 --> S3
  S3 --> S4
  S4 --> S5
  S5 --> S6
  S6 --> S7
  S7 --> S8
  S8 --> S9
  S9 --> S10
